=== NOTE on steps 4-5 (OBSERVED discrepancy, not a regression from this slice) ===
Steps 4 and 5 as literally written use --url http://example.com. The EARS-V6 Host-header
drop/accept logic itself is OBSERVED correct in both runs (step 4: dropped=[{index:0,
reason:'...host...'}]; step 5 with the Host edited to sub.example.com: dropped=[]), matching
the spec's documented Host-header assertion exactly. However the literal 'executed: 3'/
'executed: 4' + 'overall verdict BREAKER_PASS' text in steps 4/5 cannot be reproduced against
the real network, because http-probe.mjs's pre-existing, unmodified isLocalTarget gate
(DEFAULT_LOCAL_PATTERN = '^(?:localhost|127\.0\.0\.1|\[::1\])$|\.test$|\.localhost$',
scripts/resolvers/gstack-browse.mjs:25, out of this slice's scope) rejects 'example.com' as
non-local before any request is sent, so every runnable http vector's own result is
INSTRUMENT-BROKEN ('target is not local'), driving executed to 0 regardless of the Host rule.
This is intrinsic to combining --url http://example.com with the pre-existing local-only
boundary; it is not something this slice's EARS-V1-V9 work introduced or can fix without
touching an out-of-scope file. Reported here rather than silently reproduced as a false match.
